# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase ui_and_review, story SKY-006.

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. CRITICAL: Split contradicts coordinator routing note ('No elaboration or split warranted') — human confirmation required before children SKY-006-A and SKY-006-B are promoted
2. CRITICAL: Verdict format irreconcilable across child variants — legacy children (SKY-006-a, SKY-006-b) use 'Verdict: PASS' colon-prefix; promoted children (SKY-006-A-1, SKY-006-B-1) use ^(PASS|FAIL)$ bare token; human adjudication required to select canonical format before any child is implemented
3. UNRESOLVED GAP: No coverage-floor PASS gate across all child variants — GATE-TEST-RESULTS checks 0 failed/skipped/todo only; explicit human policy decision required
4. UNRESOLVED GAP: Stub test files with empty describe() blocks satisfy the three-layer coverage AC as written — no non-empty content criterion beyond file existence in some child variants
5. UNRESOLVED GAP: Async Express route handlers throwing without next(err) not covered in all child variants
6. UNRESOLVED GAP: No CORS AC under Express Safety in some child variants
7. Split children inherit all four unresolved gaps without adding new AC coverage — split did not improve completeness

Additional context from prior review: The parent story SKY-006 is a coordination envelope whose value depends entirely on the quality of its split children. The split itself (into SKY-006-A and SKY-006-B) was performed by speckit against explicit coordinator routing that said 'No elaboration or split warranted' — this contradiction requires human confirmation before children are promoted. The parent's 3-AC envelope (both children must complete, review file must satisfy children's requirements, Verdict is authoritative) is internally

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
